{"repositoryId":638088136,"availability":"available","full":"hkust-taco/superf","name":"superf","description":"Artifact for paper \"When Subtyping Constraints Liberate: A Novel Type Inference Approach for First-Class Polymorphism\" (https://popl24.sigplan.org/details/POPL-2024-popl-research-papers/50)","category":"Education","language":"Scala","stars":15,"forks":0,"created":"2023-05-09T03:58:10Z","updated":"2024-05-22T07:42:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"superf","homepage":"https://hkust-taco.github.io/superf/","topics":[],"demo":"https://hkust-taco.github.io/superf/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.471Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.471Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.471Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.471Z","stars":15,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This document follows the structure prescribed in","In this artifact, we provide a fully practical implementation of SuperF. The provided implementation is complex because it is intertwined with MLscript, a nascent functional programming language intended for real-world usage. While this has the advantage of demonstrating that our approach scales to realistic use cases and is practical for general-purpose programming, it means one needs to squint quite a bit to relate the provided implementation with the approach described in the paper.","We have reproduced here the main differences between the paper's formalism and our implementation, as stated in Appendix B:"],"features":["MLscriptF supports type-checking recursive functions, which is not shown in Section 4 for","MLscriptF does not generalize curried lambda abstractions: doing so is redundant since","MLscriptF uses explicit polymorphism levels to track extrusion and type avoidance, as described in Section 2.4. This can be seen as an optimization (to minimize the number of type","the typeTerm function of Typer.scala, which shows how to type check terms;","the constrain function of ConstraintSolver.scala, which shows how to resolve subtyping constraints (while also keeping track of a lot of meta information for better error reporting);"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hkust-taco/superf/blob/superf/README.md","fingerprint":"f03840b958504c754979170c5f8470528e1286c18762b29262a6c212c32b8605","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.654Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.654Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This document follows the structure prescribed in","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hkust-taco/superf/blob/superf/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"In this artifact, we provide a fully practical implementation of SuperF. The provided implementation is complex because it is intertwined with MLscript, a nascent functional programming language intended for real-world usage. While this has the advantage of demonstrating that our approach scales to realistic use cases and is practical for general-purpose programming, it means…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hkust-taco/superf/blob/superf/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f03840b958504c754979170c5f8470528e1286c18762b29262a6c212c32b8605","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hkust-taco/superf/blob/superf/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.655Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-05-22T07:42:48Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hkust-taco/superf/blob/superf/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T18:05:05.656Z","hash":"f03840b958504c754979170c5f8470528e1286c18762b29262a6c212c32b8605","originalBytes":22479,"storedBytes":22479,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["type","class","test","mlscript","which","types","contains","src","shared","typing","tests","diff","code","typer","implementation","corresponding","file","run","sbt","syntax","data","fcp","int","inferred","paper","types.","classes","scala","files","includes","inference","these","any","command","definition","each","level","list","main","parser","u